  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6EC9" flags="0x30">
    <title>4A 9 06 Fuel Phase (End of Ignition/Injection pulse) 32x20 -&gt; 4C04C in OneLambda</title>
    <description>I had always assumed that the values were in degrees (x10) before bdc for the end of the injection pulse. If the ecu times to the end of the pulse then rpm and tps changes will control when injection starts and the phase ensures that injection finishes before the inlet valve closes.&#013;&#010;From what I have gleaned from the synchronisation routines the ecu maintains a &quot;phase counter&quot; which runs fron 0 to 7199 as the engine turns through two revolutions. This counter is then fed to the capture/compare units to activate injection and ignition at appropriate times - all tied to the engine angle. This means the ecu has to compute times back to degrees of rotation for injection duration and ignition coil charge.&#013;&#010;</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="2" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>&#176;</units>
      <indexcount>20</indexcount>
      <outputtype>2</outputtype>
      <embedinfo type="3" linkobjid="0x3D0A" />
      <datatype>57</datatype>
      <unittype>23</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>rpm</units>
      <indexcount>32</indexcount>
      <outputtype>2</outputtype>
      <embedinfo type="3" linkobjid="0x38F3" />
      <datatype>6</datatype>
      <unittype>4</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="z">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x4A906" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedrowcount="32" mmedcolcount="20" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>&#176;BTDC</units>
      <decimalpl>1</decimalpl>
      <min>0.000000</min>
      <max>400.000000</max>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
      <MATH equation="X*2/10">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFTABLE>
